# R2 shared contract blocker: request-local rollback inside an active draft

Reported before attempting a semantics substitution. Frozen R2 was read at
revision 2, spec SHA256 `f960b64a19d208552c1423ebdf51e4dfc4aa458588c8e2ceb675c97971d1d5ed`.
The coordinator supplied R2 after the preceding candidate writer was terminal;
this writer has not edited the work order, shared source, manifests, or seeds.

The accepted public `SceneBuilder` API cannot checkpoint and restore an append
suffix inside the caller's active draft:

- `builder.rs:197` `mark` rejects every nonzero `draft_depth`.
- `builder.rs:217` `rollback` likewise rejects active drafts, even with a mark
  acquired before the draft began.
- `draft.rs:19` `begin_draft` rejects same-scene nesting: an existing scene's
  index is less than the active parent's `scene_count`.
- `draft.rs:98` `rollback_draft` consumes the entire outer token, drops the
  prefix, and ends its authorization. MEDIA only borrows that token.
- Internal checkpoint/rollback and draft validation helpers are `pub(crate)`;
  SceneBuilder storage and DraftToken fields are private outside vexel-scene.

Root needs to supply and accept a public scoped checkpoint/rollback operation
authorized by the active DraftToken for that scene. It must restore request
suffixes (images, shapes, topology, publications and accounting), preserve
prefix handles and the active outer token, and clean up unconditionally after
cancellation or allocation/admission failure. A closure transaction with these
guarantees would also suffice. MEDIA must additionally restore its text state
and cache admissions on request failure when that operation becomes available.

`tests/atomicity_gap.rs` records actual public API rejection and late image/text
failures against real lexical, animation, path, builder, draft and ledger
fixtures. These are defect reproducers, not successful atomicity proofs. No
clone/rebuild, child-scene substitution, unchecked caller cleanup, or alternate
rendering semantics are used. R2 remains blocked despite independent parity
corrections and passing scoped checks.

## Additional full-scope accounting gap

`src/svg/shape/text.c` checks and increments `builder->text_commands` against
`SVG_SHAPE_MEDIA_MAX_DOCUMENT_PATH_COMMANDS` (4 Mi commands) on every run,
including cached layouts. Accepted `vexel_scene::TextState` has cursor,
text_bytes, glyph_count and whitespace fields but no command counter;
TextDecodeRequest exposes no other document-owned text-command budget.
`TextCache.commands` is the separate 262,144-command cache admission count and
cannot substitute for document uses. The MEDIA per-layout 4 Mi check cannot
enforce the cumulative original bound.

`tests/document_budget_gap.rs` demonstrates 17 uses of a valid 262,144-command
cached fixture layout succeeding, whereas the original rejects use 17. Root
must expose a persistent document text-command budget (or equivalent accepted
per-job state) through the request contract. Its increments must participate in
the same request rollback as text_bytes/glyph_count. No cache counter is
repurposed and no new shared state has been edited by this worker.
# Accepted contract blockers (R2, before substituting behavior)

## Definition owners before geometry

`vexel-scene::DecodeOperations::plan_definition` requires `owner: ShapeId`.
`src/svg/shape/traverse.c::svg_shape_traverse_begin_opacity_group` parses the
filter before direct geometry or child traversal. A valid empty group with a
filter therefore has no ShapeId; all ShapeId fields are private and enumeration
only returns already-published real shapes. Adding a placeholder shape changes
shape counts, source maps, groups and original error priority and is forbidden.
A coordinator-owned accepted source/group owner contract is needed for this
planning stage, including empty groups. Deferring filter parsing until a first
shape exists also changes the original filter-before-geometry error priority.

## Pattern paint handoff

`PatternDescriptor` returns tile dimensions, content transform, definition and
error offset, but no resolved instance paint/mapping. The original pattern
resolver computes x/y tile origin, patternTransform inverse, user-to-base,
pixel scaling, pattern_inverse and opacity separately from content_transform
(`src/svg/shape/pattern.c:463-633`). `resolve_paint` receives only DecodeSource,
gradient PaintCache and ChargeLedger; it receives no builder or notification of
the scene-owned PatternId created after tile completion. A source-only typed
pattern paint template/handoff is needed so DECODE can insert the single-use
completion PatternId into the exact fill/stroke mapping. Content transform is
not an equivalent replacement for the missing paint mapping.

## Work quantum across accepted atomic APIs

The current DecodeSource exposes synchronous `compute_style`/`find_reference`,
and SceneBuilder exposes synchronous `append_shape`/`commit_draft` validation.
These APIs charge variable loops internally but return no resumable source-only
state. Interrupting them by WorkControl::Stop aborts or rolls back instead of
yielding; storing CssComputeSession borrowing the decoder-owned DecodeSource
would introduce a self reference. A strict total-work <= work_quantum guarantee
needs accepted resumable state, or an explicit accepted contract defining bounded
atomic operations across quantum boundaries. Reporting one token visit while
these APIs perform substantial work would be false accounting.

The worker will not change shared contracts or fabricate IDs/mappings/providers.
These blockers do not excuse missing independent style/geometry/traversal
algorithms or original pure assertions; those remain the worker's scope.

## Original close/smooth path metadata and accepted validator disagree

`tests/svg/shape/test_shape.c::main` requires successful equivalent decoding of
`M1 1 C2 2 3 3 4 4 Z S6 6 7 7` and its explicit cubic form. The accepted Rust
path parser retains the overlapping subpath records after close, matching the
original parser structure. The accepted SceneBuilder rejects overlapping
subpath ranges with InvalidArgument:0. `original_shapes.rs` preserves this
assertion and currently fails. Coordinator must reconcile accepted parser/scene
metadata contracts; decoder must not discard, rewrite or hide source metadata.

## Mask expansion post target

`PostOperation::AttachMask(MaskId)` supplies neither target GroupId nor target
shape range. Mask ownership is a group field. An Expansion contains source range,
transform, viewport, style, flavor and post only. The engine cannot choose a
real target group for this post without guessing. Direct MaskDescriptor plans
can use the known owning Finish group; the standalone post requires an accepted
explicit owner contract. The decoder reports MaskPostTarget rather than success.

## Independent unfinished parity and evidence

These interface issues do not account for all remaining work. Definition plan
expansion allocations/active stacks/child draft lists and temporary clip copying
still require comprehensive actual-capacity leases. Lower-plan flavor/post
validation and nested pattern/media/marker/gradient tests are incomplete. Root
hidden/display:none and eager animation error priority need original-order
review. Full original fuzz command-cap, cache/accounting, gradient lookup and
remaining pure predicates have not all been ported. Whole original mixed inputs
are preserved, but preserving inputs is not execution proof. Do not accept this
candidate or infer that repairing the named contracts alone completes it.
# Candidate status: incomplete

This resumed candidate preserves the earlier archived result and leaves the immutable scope catalog unchanged. Scalar sampling now uses `ControlledSampleInput` for paint-provider work and validated `JobDashView` data for stroke grid queries. A canonical fixture builds and commits a real `SceneBuilder` draft with parsed path geometry and animation, then checks same-source `RasterJob` scratch admission and canceled-growth rollback. Nine focused tests pass.

The frozen owner scope is **not complete**. Dash and grid construction still allocate standalone `DashCache` vectors, and fill rows still use `RasterScratch` vectors. Those paths do not meet same-job capacity leases, append-time source assignment, actual-capacity overlap admission, or no per-row allocation requirements. Several of the eleven original pure predicates also remain unported. No lower-engine, 603/157 oracle, or renderer-parity completion is claimed.

`accepted-job-APIcoverage.md` records the accepted owning/controlled interfaces. One exact safe-composition gap is recorded in parity-map.json: `JobDashView` immutably borrows the job while all same-job buffer mutation requires `&mut RasterJob`; per-sample revalidation changes work accounting. The coordinator owns any shared repair. After that repair, crate-owned cache/fill adaptation and the remaining pure predicates still need completion, followed by independent review and fresh main checks.
//! One bounded request scope inside the current draft. Marks own no prefix data.
//! Discarding a token does not commit: explicitly abort with the outer draft.
use crate::{
    types::{invalid, stopped},
    *,
};
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct RequestToken {
    scene: SceneId,
    draft: u64,
    nonce: u64,
    generation: u64,
}
#[derive(Debug)]
pub(crate) struct ActiveRequest {
    token: RequestToken,
    pub(crate) mark: BuildMark,
    scene_count: usize,
    ignored: [Ignored; 4],
}
impl SceneBuilder {
    pub(crate) fn request_protects_draft(&self, draft: &DraftToken) -> bool {
        self.request
            .as_ref()
            .is_some_and(|r| r.token.draft == draft.nonce)
    }
    pub(crate) fn request_protects_scene(&self, id: SceneId) -> bool {
        self.request
            .as_ref()
            .is_some_and(|r| id.index() < r.scene_count)
    }
    pub(crate) fn request_identity(&self) -> Option<RequestToken> {
        self.request.as_ref().map(|r| r.token)
    }
    pub fn begin_request(
        &mut self,
        draft: &DraftToken,
        control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
    ) -> Result<RequestToken> {
        self.draft_index(draft)?;
        if self.request.is_some() {
            return Err(invalid(0));
        }
        control.checkpoint().map_err(stopped)?;
        let token = RequestToken {
            scene: draft.mark.scene,
            draft: draft.nonce,
            nonce: self.serial()?,
            generation: self.generation,
        };
        let mark = self.checkpoint_internal(token.scene)?;
        self.request = Some(ActiveRequest {
            token,
            mark,
            scene_count: self.scenes.len(),
            ignored: self.ignored,
        });
        Ok(token)
    }
    fn request_index(&self, draft: &DraftToken, token: RequestToken) -> Result<usize> {
        let i = self.draft_index(draft)?;
        let active = self.request.as_ref().ok_or_else(|| invalid(0))?;
        if active.token != token
            || token.draft != draft.nonce
            || token.scene != draft.mark.scene
            || token.generation != self.generation
        {
            return Err(invalid(0));
        }
        Ok(i)
    }
    /// Failure leaves the request active for unconditional cleanup. Prefix handles
    /// retain their insertion serials; no whole-scene epoch is an ID authority.
    pub fn commit_request(
        &mut self,
        draft: &DraftToken,
        token: RequestToken,
        control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
    ) -> Result<()> {
        self.request_index(draft, token)?;
        control.checkpoint().map_err(stopped)?;
        crate::validate::scene(self, token.scene, control)?;
        self.request = None;
        Ok(())
    }
    pub fn rollback_request(&mut self, draft: &DraftToken, token: RequestToken) -> Result<()> {
        let i = self.request_index(draft, token)?;
        let active = self.request.as_ref().ok_or_else(|| invalid(0))?;
        let mut released = 0;
        for scene in &self.scenes[active.scene_count..] {
            released = crate::memory::add(released, scene.storage_bytes()?)?;
        }
        // Prevalidate cleanup arithmetic before taking the checkpoint.
        self.scenes[i]
            .epoch
            .checked_add(1)
            .ok_or_else(crate::memory::arithmetic)?;
        let active = self.request.take().ok_or_else(|| invalid(0))?;
        let mut mark = active.mark;
        mark.epoch = self.scenes[i].epoch;
        self.rollback_internal(mark)?;
        self.scenes.truncate(active.scene_count);
        self.stats.live_bytes -= released;
        self.ignored = active.ignored;
        Ok(())
    }
    /// Recover an abandoned token. Only the same still-active outer draft can
    /// abort. No control polling, allocation, implicit commit or Drop callback.
    pub fn abort_request(&mut self, draft: &DraftToken) -> Result<()> {
        self.draft_index(draft)?;
        let token = self.request.as_ref().ok_or_else(|| invalid(0))?.token;
        self.rollback_request(draft, token)
    }
}
//! Additive production delegates. Legacy DecodeOperations remains an explicit
//! owned-fixture interface; no blanket conversion or default backend exists.
use crate::{
    types::{invalid, stopped},
    *,
};
use vexel_xml::XmlSpan;
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]
pub enum DefinitionTarget {
    Shape(ShapeId),
    Group(GroupId),
}
/// Same active scene/draft/source-token owner, not a naked slot or fake shape.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]
pub struct DefinitionOwner {
    scene: SceneId,
    draft: u64,
    generation: u64,
    target: DefinitionTarget,
    element: ElementId,
}
impl DefinitionOwner {
    pub fn target(self) -> DefinitionTarget {
        self.target
    }
    pub fn element(self) -> ElementId {
        self.element
    }
    pub fn validate(self, ctx: &DefinitionContext<'_, '_>) -> Result<()> {
        ctx.validate()?;
        let active = ctx.builder.active_draft().ok_or_else(|| invalid(0))?;
        if ctx.scene != self.scene
            || active.scene != self.scene
            || active.nonce != self.draft
            || ctx.builder.generation != self.generation
        {
            return Err(invalid(0));
        }
        let view = ctx.builder.scene(self.scene)?;
        match self.target {
            DefinitionTarget::Shape(id) if view.shape(id).is_some() => Ok(()),
            DefinitionTarget::Group(id) if view.group(id).is_some() => Ok(()),
            _ => Err(invalid(0)),
        }
    }
}
impl SceneBuilder {
    pub fn definition_owner(
        &self,
        draft: &DraftToken,
        source: &DecodeSource<'_>,
        element: ElementId,
        target: DefinitionTarget,
        control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
    ) -> Result<DefinitionOwner> {
        self.draft_index(draft)?;
        if !std::sync::Arc::ptr_eq(self.source_owner(), source.source_owner()) {
            return Err(invalid(0));
        }
        source.element(element, crate::memory::add(element.0, 1)?, control)?;
        let view = self.scene(draft.mark.scene)?;
        match target {
            DefinitionTarget::Shape(id) if view.shape(id).is_some() => {}
            DefinitionTarget::Group(id) if view.group(id).is_some() => {}
            _ => return Err(invalid(0)),
        }
        Ok(DefinitionOwner {
            scene: draft.mark.scene,
            draft: draft.nonce,
            generation: self.generation,
            target,
            element,
        })
    }
    /// Atomic owning filter publication on a real (possibly empty) group. The
    /// child range is finalized later using the same guarded draft mutator.
    pub fn publish_group_filter(
        &mut self,
        draft: &DraftToken,
        owner: DefinitionOwner,
        filter: Filter,
        primitives: &[FilterPrimitive],
        control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
    ) -> Result<FilterId> {
        let i = self.draft_index(draft)?;
        if owner.scene != draft.mark.scene
            || owner.draft != draft.nonce
            || owner.generation != self.generation
        {
            return Err(invalid(0));
        }
        let DefinitionTarget::Group(group) = owner.target else {
            return Err(invalid(0));
        };
        self.draft_slot(draft, 9, group.index(), self.scenes[i].groups.len())?;
        let mut value = *self
            .scene(owner.scene)?
            .group(group)
            .ok_or_else(|| invalid(0))?;
        let mut mark = self.checkpoint_internal(owner.scene)?;
        let result = (|| {
            let id = self.append_filter(owner.scene, filter, primitives, control)?;
            value.filter = Some(id);
            self.finalize_group(draft, group, value, control)?;
            Ok(id)
        })();
        if result.is_err() {
            mark.epoch = self.scenes[i].epoch;
            self.rollback_internal(mark)?;
        }
        result
    }
}
/// Stops borrow the resolver cache, independently of temporary source/ledger
/// borrows. The resolver owns/meters its cache; this result owns no stop Vec.
#[derive(Debug)]
pub enum CachedPaint<'cache> {
    Plain(Paint),
    Gradient {
        template: &'cache GradientTemplateId,
        paint: Paint,
        stops: &'cache [PaintStop],
    },
}
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum PaintChannel {
    Fill,
    Stroke,
}
impl SceneBuilder {
    pub fn append_cached_paint(
        &mut self,
        scene: SceneId,
        cached: CachedPaint<'_>,
        channel: PaintChannel,
        control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
    ) -> Result<usize> {
        match cached {
            CachedPaint::Gradient {
                template,
                paint,
                stops,
            } => match channel {
                PaintChannel::Fill => {
                    self.append_template_fill(scene, template, paint, stops, control)
                }
                PaintChannel::Stroke => {
                    self.append_template_stroke(scene, template, paint, stops, control)
                }
            },
            CachedPaint::Plain(paint) => {
                if matches!(paint.kind, PaintKind::Linear | PaintKind::Radial)
                    || paint.stops != TableRange::EMPTY
                {
                    return Err(invalid(0));
                }
                match channel {
                    PaintChannel::Fill => self.append_fill_paint(scene, paint, control),
                    PaintChannel::Stroke => self.append_stroke_paint(scene, paint, control),
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
pub trait CachedPaintResolver {
    fn resolve_cached<'cache>(
        &'cache mut self,
        source: &mut DecodeSource<'_>,
        ledger: &mut ChargeLedger,
        value: XmlSpan,
        edges: &[Edge],
        inverse: Affine,
        viewport: [f64; 2],
        control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
    ) -> Result<CachedPaint<'cache>>;
}
/// Actual shared resolve+publication operation; resolver output is used directly.
pub fn resolve_publish_cached(
    resolver: &mut dyn CachedPaintResolver,
    source: &mut DecodeSource<'_>,
    ledger: &mut ChargeLedger,
    builder: &mut SceneBuilder,
    scene: SceneId,
    value: XmlSpan,
    edges: &[Edge],
    inverse: Affine,
    viewport: [f64; 2],
    channel: PaintChannel,
    control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
) -> Result<usize> {
    ledger.require_owner(ledger.owner_identity(), source.source_owner())?;
    if !std::sync::Arc::ptr_eq(builder.source_owner(), source.source_owner()) {
        return Err(invalid(0));
    }
    builder.writable(scene)?;
    if value.slice(source.source()).is_none() {
        return Err(invalid(value.offset));
    }
    control.checkpoint().map_err(stopped)?;
    let cached =
        resolver.resolve_cached(source, ledger, value, edges, inverse, viewport, control)?;
    builder.append_cached_paint(scene, cached, channel, control)
}
#[derive(Debug)]
pub enum ProductionDefinitionPlan<'src> {
    Definition(DefinitionPlan<'src>),
    Pattern {
        plan: DefinitionPlan<'src>,
        mapping: PatternMapping,
    },
}
/// Every operation is required. Implementations may share lower functions with
/// fixtures explicitly, but cannot silently inherit their owned paint path.
pub trait DefinitionPlanner {
    fn plan_owned_definition<'src>(
        &mut self,
        ctx: &mut DefinitionContext<'src, '_>,
        kind: DefinitionKind,
        element: ElementId,
        owner: DefinitionOwner,
        transform: Affine,
        bounds: [f64; 4],
        style: &CssPaint<'src>,
        control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
    ) -> Result<ProductionDefinitionPlan<'src>>;
}
pub trait MediaDecodeOperations {
    fn decode_text(
        &mut self,
        request: TextDecodeRequest<'_, '_>,
        builder: &mut SceneBuilder,
        control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
    ) -> Result<bool>;
    fn decode_image(
        &mut self,
        request: ImageDecodeRequest<'_, '_>,
        builder: &mut SceneBuilder,
        control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
    ) -> Result<ShapeId>;
}
pub trait ProductionDecodeOperations:
    CachedPaintResolver + DefinitionPlanner + MediaDecodeOperations
{
}
pub trait ProductionDecodeSession {
    fn step<'s>(
        &'s mut self,
        quantum: u64,
        operations: &mut dyn ProductionDecodeOperations,
        control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
    ) -> Result<DecodeEvent<'s>>;
    fn resume_pattern(
        &mut self,
        ticket: PatternTicket,
        job: &mut RasterJob,
        result: Result<JobRenderOutput>,
        control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
    ) -> Result<()>;
    fn finish(self, control: &mut dyn WorkControl) -> Result<SceneGraph>
    where
        Self: Sized;
}
/// Validate typed owner before entering the lower planner and require its entire
/// computed pattern mapping at return. This performs no legacy owned conversion.
/// The lower adapter owns/admit/releases its plan/cache allocations via ctx.ledger.
pub fn plan_production_definition<'src>(
    planner: &mut dyn DefinitionPlanner,
    ctx: &mut DefinitionContext<'src, '_>,
    kind: DefinitionKind,
    element: ElementId,
    owner: DefinitionOwner,
    transform: Affine,
    bounds: [f64; 4],
    style: &CssPaint<'src>,
    control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
) -> Result<ProductionDefinitionPlan<'src>> {
    owner.validate(ctx)?;
    validate_style(ctx.shared.source(), style, control)?;
    ctx.shared
        .element(element, crate::memory::add(element.0, 1)?, control)?;
    if !vexel_geometry::affine_valid(transform)
        || !bounds.into_iter().all(f64::is_finite)
        || bounds[2] < 0.
        || bounds[3] < 0.
    {
        return Err(invalid(0));
    }
    let plan = planner
        .plan_owned_definition(ctx, kind, element, owner, transform, bounds, style, control)?;
    let (definition, mapping) = match &plan {
        ProductionDefinitionPlan::Definition(plan) => (plan, None),
        ProductionDefinitionPlan::Pattern { plan, mapping } => (plan, Some(*mapping)),
    };
    let actual = match &definition.descriptor {
        DefinitionDescriptor::Clip(_) => DefinitionKind::Clip,
        DefinitionDescriptor::Mask(_) => DefinitionKind::Mask,
        DefinitionDescriptor::Pattern(descriptor) => {
            if descriptor.definition != element {
                return Err(invalid(0));
            }
            let map = mapping.ok_or_else(|| invalid(0))?;
            map.pixel_inverse(*descriptor)?;
            let DefinitionTarget::Shape(shape) = owner.target else {
                return Err(invalid(0));
            };
            if ctx
                .builder
                .scene(ctx.scene)?
                .shape(shape)
                .ok_or_else(|| invalid(0))?
                .source
                != map.source_map
                || map.bounds != bounds
            {
                return Err(invalid(0));
            }
            DefinitionKind::Pattern
        }
        DefinitionDescriptor::Marker(_) => DefinitionKind::Marker,
        DefinitionDescriptor::Filter { filter, primitives } => {
            let DefinitionTarget::Group(_) = owner.target else {
                return Err(invalid(0));
            };
            crate::validate::filter(*filter, primitives, control)?;
            for p in primitives {
                control.charge(WorkKind::FilterPixel, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
                if p.source_offset > ctx.shared.source().len() {
                    return Err(invalid(p.source_offset));
                }
            }
            DefinitionKind::Filter
        }
    };
    if actual != kind || (kind != DefinitionKind::Pattern && mapping.is_some()) {
        return Err(invalid(0));
    }
    if definition.expansions.len() > 65536 {
        return Err(crate::types::limit(LimitKind::References));
    }
    for expansion in &definition.expansions {
        control
            .charge(WorkKind::ReferenceProbe, 1)
            .map_err(stopped)?;
        expansion.range.require(ctx.shared.tokens().len(), 0)?;
        validate_style(ctx.shared.source(), &expansion.style, control)?;
        if !vexel_geometry::affine_valid(expansion.transform)
            || !expansion
                .viewport
                .into_iter()
                .all(|v| v.is_finite() && v > 0.)
        {
            return Err(invalid(0));
        }
    }
    control.checkpoint().map_err(stopped)?;
    Ok(plan)
}

fn validate_style(
    source: &[u8],
    style: &CssPaint<'_>,
    control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
) -> Result<()> {
    for property in vexel_svg_css::Property::ALL {
        control.charge(WorkKind::PaintVisit, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
        if let Some(value) = style.value(property) {
            let bytes = value
                .span
                .slice(source)
                .ok_or_else(|| invalid(value.span.offset))?;
            if bytes.as_ptr() != value.bytes.as_ptr() || bytes.len() != value.bytes.len() {
                return Err(invalid(value.span.offset));
            }
        }
    }
    Ok(())
}

//! Borrowed engine inputs: scalar math reads the original element types, never
//! copies a cache into unmetered Vecs. Descriptors own no nested allocation.
use crate::types::{invalid, limit, stopped};
use crate::*;

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]
pub struct JobDashRange {
    pub segments: TableRange,
    pub joins: TableRange,
    pub grid_cells: JobBuffer<GridCell>,
    pub grid_refs: JobBuffer<u32>,
    pub grid_min_x: f64,
    pub grid_min_y: f64,
    pub grid_cell_size: f64,
    pub grid_columns: u16,
    pub grid_rows: u16,
}
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]
pub struct JobDashCache {
    pub segments: JobBuffer<DashSegment>,
    pub joins: JobBuffer<DashJoin>,
    pub shapes: JobBuffer<JobDashRange>,
    pub build_steps: usize,
}
#[derive(Clone, Copy)]
pub struct JobDashView<'a> {
    job: &'a RasterJob,
    pub segments: &'a [DashSegment],
    pub joins: &'a [DashJoin],
    pub shapes: &'a [JobDashRange],
}
impl RasterJob {
    pub fn dash_view(&self, cache: JobDashCache, control: &mut dyn WorkControl) -> Result<JobDashView<'_>> {
        control.checkpoint().map_err(stopped)?;
        if cache.build_steps > 1_000_000 {
            return Err(limit(LimitKind::DashCache));
        }
        self.require_pool(cache.segments, RasterPool::Dash)?;
        self.require_pool(cache.joins, RasterPool::Dash)?;
        self.require_pool(cache.shapes, RasterPool::Dash)?;
        let view = JobDashView {
            job: self,
            segments: self.slice(cache.segments)?,
            joins: self.slice(cache.joins)?,
            shapes: self.slice(cache.shapes)?,
        };
        view.validate(control)?;
        Ok(view)
    }
}
impl<'a> JobDashView<'a> {
    /// Resolves only same-job, still-live handles. A caller may retain descriptors
    /// across release, but can never dereference them without revalidation.
    pub fn grid(&self, range: &JobDashRange) -> Result<(&'a [GridCell], &'a [u32])> {
        self.job.require_pool(range.grid_cells, RasterPool::Grid)?;
        self.job.require_pool(range.grid_refs, RasterPool::Grid)?;
        Ok((
            self.job.slice(range.grid_cells)?,
            self.job.slice(range.grid_refs)?,
        ))
    }
    pub fn validate(&self, control: &mut dyn WorkControl) -> Result<()> {
        if self.shapes.len() > 65536 {
            return Err(limit(LimitKind::Shapes));
        }
        for segment in self.segments {
            control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
            if ![segment.edge.a, segment.edge.b]
                .into_iter()
                .all(vexel_geometry::finite_point)
            {
                return Err(invalid(0));
            }
        }
        for join in self.joins {
            control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
            if ![join.previous, join.vertex, join.next]
                .into_iter()
                .all(vexel_geometry::finite_point)
            {
                return Err(invalid(0));
            }
        }
        let (mut cell_count, mut ref_count) = (0usize, 0usize);
        for range in self.shapes {
            control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
            range.segments.require(self.segments.len(), 0)?;
            range.joins.require(self.joins.len(), 0)?;
            let (cells, refs) = self.grid(range)?;
            cell_count = cell_count
                .checked_add(cells.len())
                .ok_or_else(crate::memory::arithmetic)?;
            ref_count = ref_count
                .checked_add(refs.len())
                .ok_or_else(crate::memory::arithmetic)?;
            if cell_count > 65536
                || ref_count > 1_000_000
                || range.grid_columns > 128
                || range.grid_rows > 128
            {
                return Err(limit(LimitKind::Grid));
            }
            if ![range.grid_min_x, range.grid_min_y, range.grid_cell_size]
                .into_iter()
                .all(f64::is_finite)
                || cells.len() != range.grid_columns as usize * range.grid_rows as usize
                || ((cells.is_empty()) != (range.grid_columns == 0 && range.grid_rows == 0))
                || (!cells.is_empty() && range.grid_cell_size <= 0.0)
            {
                return Err(invalid(0));
            }
            for cell in cells {
                control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
                TableRange {
                    first: cell.first,
                    count: cell.count,
                }
                .require(refs.len(), 0)?;
            }
            for reference in refs {
                control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
                let index = (*reference & !STROKE_GRID_JOIN_BIT) as usize;
                let allowed = if *reference & STROKE_GRID_JOIN_BIT != 0 {
                    range.joins
                } else {
                    range.segments
                };
                if index < allowed.first || index >= allowed.end().ok_or_else(crate::memory::arithmetic)? {
                    return Err(invalid(0));
                }
            }
        }
        control.checkpoint().map_err(stopped)
    }
}

